#. box title
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1557
msgid "Advanced: month names and the language"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1558
msgid "`%b` and `%B` follow the **locale**. By default Python uses English month names, but if a program (or a library) switches the locale with [`locale.setlocale`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/locale.html#locale.setlocale), `%b` expects the month names of that language, and [`strptime(\"8 Jun 2014\", \"%d %b %Y\")`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime.strptime) can fail. For data, prefer numeric formats. If a source has English month names, a small dictionary `{\"Jan\": 1, ...}` ([session 6](./06-dictionaries.md)) is the safe way."
msgstr ""

